  "body": "## Finding description and impact\nconvertToShares truncates the shares returned to depositors. This means after any realistic deposit, totalAssets is strictly greater than `HALF_SLOPE * totalShares²` by 1-2 wei. When anyone calls `previewWithdraw(totalAssets, totalAssets, totalShares)`, the internal PRBMath subtraction underflows and reverts\nWhen depositing assets, _convertToShares computes the corresponding shares by taking a floor square root\n```solidity\nUD60x18 inner = add(PCMath.square(s), div(wrap(assets), HALF_SLOPE));\nUD60x18 sharesUD = sub(sqrt(inner), s); \nshares = unwrap(sharesUD);\n```\nBecause the sqrt operation floors the result, the vault retains slightly more assets than the  curve requires\nSince minDeposit = 1e16, virtually every real deposit produces non-round shares and creates this gap instantly.(Note this is submitted assuming it will be used like a helper)\n## Impact\n- Triggers after the first realistic deposit\n- Any function using(inherting) totalAssets to previewWithdraw always reverts\n- Funds are not lost —redeem(totalShares) continues to work  but the entire withdraw path is broken from first use\n\n\n## Recommended mitigation steps\n\nAdd a boundary guard in previewWithdraw in both contracts before the subtraction:",
  "proof_of_concept": "Paste this test in the given test suite file `BondingCurveRegistry.t.sol` and run it with \n`forge test --mt test_previewWithdrawReverts -vvv`\n```solidity \nfunction test_previewWithdrawreverts() public {\n    // Step 1: Simulate a real deposit - get shares from depositing 3e18 assets into empty vault\n    uint256 depositAssets = 3e18;\n    uint256 sharesOut = progressiveCurve.previewDeposit(depositAssets, 0, 0);\n\n    // Step 2: Vault state after deposit\n    uint256 totalShares = sharesOut;\n    uint256 totalAssets = depositAssets;\n\n    // Step 3: Confirm dust gap exists\n    // _convertToShares floors sqrt → HALF_SLOPE * totalShares² < totalAssets\n    uint256 redeemable = progressiveCurve.previewRedeem(totalShares, totalShares, totalAssets);\n    assertLt(redeemable, totalAssets, \"no dust gap\");\n\n    // Step 4: previewWithdraw(totalAssets) reverts\n    // divUp(totalAssets, HALF_SLOPE) > square(totalShares) → PRBMath underflow\n    vm.expectRevert();\n    progressiveCurve.previewWithdraw(totalAssets, totalAssets, totalShares);\n}\n```",
